  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output A.1. More accurate and sustainable statistics on decent work using the latest statistical standards</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">With the contribution of RBSA, the Central Statistical Organization in Iraq (CSO) and the Kurdistan Region Statistics Office (KRSO) conducted a pilot survey followed by fieldwork/ data collection, the latter completed in August 2021.

After cleaning the microdata, results of the survey are expected to be available in December 2021.

Both CSO and KRSO carried-out and assessed pilot test results.

Both CSO and KRSO carried-out the Labour Force Survey (LFS) following latest statistical standards and methods and improved questionnaires.

Based on the information provided by the Iraq LFS through its questionnaire, the ILO will increase the reporting of several SDG indicators under the ILO&apos;s custodianship.
 The ILO adapted the Iraq LFS questionnaire inline with the 20th ICLS, and provided technical support in microdata review to ensure an enhanced quality and quantity of data. 

The ILO provided capacity building to the CSO and KRSO staff to equip them with the know-how to be able to conduct regular surveys in the future for subsequent policy making, monitoring and evaluation.

The ILO supported the CSO and KRSO in developing a labour force survey questionnaire in line with the latest ILO guidelines and recommendations, in addition to providing support to all preparatory work.

The ILO provided technical support in questionnaire design and questionnaire testing.

The ILO provided capacity building and technical support via the organization of IT trainings in for the implementation of the CsPro.

The ILO provided technical support in pilot testing.</narrative>
   </description>
